  "steps": [
    "To a bowl add 60g Greek yogurt, 1 tbsp ginger garlic paste, 1 tsp red chilli, 1 tsp garam masala, 1/4 tsp turmeric, 1 tbsp Kasuri methi (magic herbs), 1 tsp salt.",
    "Mix 200g low fat paneer in there, coat it nicely and set it aside.",
    "Make the mint chutney by adding the following ingredients in a blender: handful of coriander, handful of mint, 1 tsp cumin seeds, 1 tsp chilli powder, 2 garlic cloves, 5g ginger, half a lime juice (10ml), 1/4 tsp salt, 80ml water.",
    "Blend it well and set it aside.",
    "Now to a pan set to medium-high heat. Add 1 tsp ghee, 1 sliced onion, 1/2 a pepper (slices), 1 tsp salt, and cook for three to four minutes until the onions turn translucent.",
    "Add marinated paneer and cook for another three to four minutes and set it aside.",
    "For the wrap I’m using a frozen chapati.",
    "Topping it with a layer of our mint chutney, the cooked paneer, top with freshly chopped cilantro, squeeze of lime, wrap it nice and tight and it’s ready to eat."
  ],
